Executive Summary
This project delivers a robust, interactive Excel dashboard analyzing customer shopping data from Istanbul malls spanning 2021 to 2023. It enables quick insights into sales revenue, product category performance, payment trends, and shopper demographic behaviors. The dashboard supports rapid decision-making through intuitive filters and clear KPIs, addressing key retail questions with actionable analytics.

Introduction
Retail businesses require timely, data-driven insight into transaction patterns to optimize operations and marketing. This report outlines the development process and key outcomes of an Excel-based portfolio dashboard designed to analyze transaction data from multiple shopping malls, providing executives an accessible overview and drill-down capabilities.

Data Description
The dataset consists of 99,457 retail transactions from Kaggle, including variables such as invoice number, customer demographics (age, gender), product categories, quantities, prices, payment methods, and invoice dates. Data spans a three-year period enabling temporal trend analysis.

Objectives
Engineer a clean, user-friendly dashboard summarizing revenue, transaction volume, and product mix

Incorporate interactive filtering by time, customer age group, gender, shopping mall, category, and payment method

Enable rapid business insights without complex formula use or technical expertise

Methodology
Comprehensive data cleaning ensured consistent date formatting and created custom demographic bins for age groups. PivotTables, PivotCharts, slicers, and timelines in Excel  structured the dashboard, with calculated KPIs reflecting total revenue, transaction counts, and average transaction values. A distinct customer identification logic supports repeat purchase analysis.

Key Findings
Electronics and apparel categories dominate revenue share, with seasonal spikes observed during key months

Payment preferences vary notably across demographics, with younger groups favoring digital payments

Female shoppers show significant spending contributions within fashion categories

Repeat purchase behavior highlights core loyal customer segments

Conclusion and Recommendations
This dashboard exemplifies how business intelligence tools can transform complex retail data into clear visual narratives supporting decision-making. Future improvements may include extending analysis across new retail locations, integrating additional customer behavioral data, and automating data refresh workflows.
